# Line endings, decided here rather than by whoever clones.
#
# The install path is a shell script and the deployment target is Linux. A
# checkout on a machine with `core.autocrlf=true` — the Windows default —
# rewrites these with CRLF, and then the box answers `bash: $'\r': command not
# found` on the first line of the shebang. That failure names nothing useful
# and costs an evening.
#
# This is not a style preference. Everything below is a file some other program
# parses byte by byte.

*.sh            text eol=lf
.githooks/*     text eol=lf
*.service       text eol=lf
*.timer         text eol=lf
*.conf          text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile    text eol=lf
.env.example    text eol=lf
alembic.ini     text eol=lf

# Statements and archives. Never touched, never diffed — a "helpful"
# normalisation pass over a PDF or a gzip is corruption.
*.pdf           binary
*.tar.gz        binary
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
